{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"recent-wholesome-fulmar","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`import rebar` callers get a return value, not a terminal, so the first-class way to raise\na non-fatal warning is Python's dedicated **`warnings`** subsystem (not `logging`, which is\nsilent unless the app configures it, and which the brainstorm explicitly rejected as \"log\nonly\"). This story emits a `warnings.warn` of a dedicated category from single-ticket\nlibrary functions when the detector fires.\n\nDepends on the detector (`cross_session_warning_for`, sibling story) and the reducer\nclearing.\n\n## Approach\n\nDefine a dedicated warning category `class CrossSessionWarning(UserWarning)` (exported from\nthe package, e.g. `rebar.CrossSessionWarning`) so callers can filter/escalate it precisely\nwith the stdlib `warnings` filters. In each single-ticket library entry point, call\n`cross_session_warning_for(ticket_id, ...)` and, when it returns a string, `warnings.warn(msg,\nCrossSessionWarning, stacklevel=2)` before returning; when it returns `None`, do nothing (no\nwarning emitted).\n\nSingle-ticket library functions to cover (mirroring the CLI/MCP allowlist): the read\n`show_ticket` (`src/rebar/_lib_reads.py:40`) and `deps`; the writes `transition` / `reopen`\n(`src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:272`/`:455`), `comment`, `edit`, `tag`, `untag`,\n`set_file_impact`, `declare_no_file_impact`, `link` (primary endpoint), `unlink` (primary\nendpoint), `archive`. Bulk reads (`list_tickets`, `search`, `ready`, `next_batch`) do **not**\nwarn. `claim` is excluded (an already-`in_progress` ticket raises `ConcurrencyError` before\nany warning path). No function's return type changes — the warning rides the `warnings`\nchannel, matching the \"all surfaces first-class without a return-shape change\" decision.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A small module or the package `__init__` for the `CrossSessionWarning` category export.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py` — emit in `show_ticket` and `deps`.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` — emit in the single-ticket write functions listed above.\n- `docs/reuse-surface.md` — document `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` and that single-ticket\n  library functions emit it (and bulk reads do not).\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **in-process unit test** using the stdlib `warnings` capture (`pytest.warns` /\n`warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)`) — the mechanism is entirely in-process\n(test-design §3 pure/validation path). Real temporary tracker; acting session set via\n`REBAR_SESSION_ID`.\n\n- With a ticket held by session A and acting session B, `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` emits\n  exactly one `CrossSessionWarning` whose message names holder `A`; assert the same for one\n  write, e.g. `rebar.comment(<id>, \"x\")`.\n- Negative control (same session): acting as A, assert **no** `CrossSessionWarning` is\n  emitted (`catch_warnings(record=True)` list is empty of that category).\n- Bulk exclusion: `rebar.list_tickets()` / `rebar.ready()` as B emit no `CrossSessionWarning`.\n- Unset-id silence: with `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` emits none.\n- Category precision: the emitted warning is an instance of `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` (a\n  `UserWarning` subclass), so a caller can filter it distinctly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` and `rebar.comment(<id>, ...)` each emit exactly one\n  `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` naming holder `A` when acting as session B against an A-held\n  ticket (checked by a `pytest.warns` test under `make test`).\n- [ ] Negative control: acting as session A, no `CrossSessionWarning` is emitted by those\n  functions (checked by `catch_warnings(record=True)` asserting none of that category).\n- [ ] `rebar.list_tickets()` and `rebar.ready()` as session B emit no `CrossSessionWarning`\n  for A's `in_progress` ticket (checked by a bulk-exclusion assertion).\n- [ ] With `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` emits no `CrossSessionWarning`\n  (checked by an unset-id assertion).\n- [ ] The emitted warning is an instance of `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` subclassing\n  `UserWarning` (checked by an `isinstance` assertion in the warns test).\n- [ ] `docs/reuse-surface.md` documents `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` and the single-ticket\n  emission (checked: `grep -n \"CrossSessionWarning\" docs/reuse-surface.md` matches).","id":"3d8a-5a5d-8773-473d","parent_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Library: warnings.warn CrossSessionWarning from single-ticket functions"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787866557605990730,"uuid":"79a7beb7-aaca-42dc-aad0-e650db996952"}